6. The four real chain/CMS measurements use purpose `any`; the separate VHN key-usage test includes criteria and expected result. Synthetic attime {attime} falls inside all three measured certificate validity intervals. All {len(negmut)} negative/mutation controls specify a failure reason in the test matrix. The signature mutation parses, the distinct malformed fixture is refused, and no suppression flag was found. The synthetic entitlement control uses `smimesign` by construction.

7. Rehearsal exited {reh.returncode}, reported {pass_ready} `PASS_READY` phases, and left progress unchanged at `{before}`.

8. Runtime self-tests: {tests['selftest_runtime']['tests_run']} run, {tests['selftest_runtime']['failures']} failures, {tests['selftest_runtime']['errors']} errors, {tests['selftest_runtime']['skips']} skips. Package tests: {tests['package_tests']['tests_run']} run, {tests['package_tests']['failures']} failures, {tests['package_tests']['errors']} errors, {tests['package_tests']['skips']} skips.

9. The packaged safety review exited {sr.returncode}, reported clean true, zero findings, and zero unpermitted changes. Independent AST inspection found {len(findings)} forbidden constructs or nonconforming `subprocess.run` calls and {len(write_r456)} write references targeting R4/R5/R6.

10. References manifest: {len(ref_rows)} records, {len(ref_missing)} missing, {len(ref_bad)} mismatched. Four staged CA certificates each have a DER-identical match in references and operator intake. `REF-08-TL-DE.xml` hashes to `{xml_digest}`, matching the published digest.

11. Live results/evidence contain {len(result_seals) + len(evidence_seals)} seals and {len(result_plans) + len(evidence_plans)} plans. MODE is `{mode_bytes.decode(errors='replace').rstrip()}`.

## Unresolved findings

{('None.' if not FAIL else '\n'.join('- ' + x for x in FAIL))}

Every requested claim was established by direct measurement or executable-code inspection. Detailed values and command-output hashes are in the companion JSON files.
"""

(HERE / "VERIFICATION_RESULT.json").write_text(json.dumps(result, indent=2) + "\n")
(HERE / "MEASUREMENTS.json").write_text(json.dumps(M, indent=2, sort_keys=True) + "\n")
